            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for expensive, then the Urdu for cheap."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: اونچا",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اونچا — ū̃chā — \"high\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اونچا (ū̃chā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from ucca, \"tall, lofty\" (CDIAL 1634). CDIAL calls the influence of udañc, \"turned upwards\", on the nasal very doubtful."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
